# The route table (docs/design/12-routing.md, docs/compiler/codegen.md §14).
# Every page prints its parsed parameters, so a match is visible in the body.

### a named root URL serves its page
GET /
>>> 200
~ landing page

### a page without `at` is at its kebab-case name
GET /pricing
>>> 200
~ pricing page

### a multi-word page name becomes kebab case
GET /sign-up-flow
>>> 200
~ sign up flow page

### the camel-case spelling of a kebab URL is not a route
GET /signUpFlow
>>> 404

### unknown query parameters are ignored
GET /pricing?utm_source=mail&x=1
>>> 200
~ pricing page

### a required Int parameter is a path segment
GET /product/42
>>> 200
~ product 42
~ tab overview

### a negative Int parses
GET /product/-7
>>> 200
~ product -7

### a parameter that isn't an Int is a 404
GET /product/forty-two
>>> 404

### a decimal is not an Int
GET /product/4.2
>>> 404

### an Int outside the safe range is a 404, not a wrong page
GET /product/99999999999999999999
>>> 404

### a missing required parameter is a 404
GET /product
>>> 404

### an extra path segment is not the page
GET /product/42/extra
>>> 404

### an optional enum parameter is read from the query by case name
GET /product/42?tab=reviews
>>> 200
~ tab reviews

### an unknown enum case in the query is a 404
GET /product/42?tab=specs
>>> 404

### an enum case in the wrong letter case is a 404
GET /product/42?tab=Reviews
>>> 404

### an optional parameter at its default is omitted from links
GET /product/42
>>> 200
~ href="/product/42"
~ href="/product/42?tab=reviews"

### a named URL with a static suffix wins over shorter templates
GET /product/42/reviews
>>> 200
~ reviews of product 42

### links to a named URL use its template
GET /product/9
>>> 200
~ href="/product/9/reviews"

### a static segment wins over a parameter in the same position
GET /posts/new
>>> 200
~ new post form
!~ post new

### the parameter matches every other value
GET /posts/hello-world
>>> 200
~ post hello-world

### a Uuid parameter parses a UUID
GET /item/0b6f3c8e-2d4a-4f1b-9c3e-5a7d8e9f0a1b
>>> 200
~ item 0b6f3c8e-2d4a-4f1b-9c3e-5a7d8e9f0a1b

### a malformed Uuid is a 404
GET /item/not-a-uuid
>>> 404

### a Uuid with a missing group is a 404
GET /item/0b6f3c8e-2d4a-4f1b-9c3e
>>> 404

### two required parameters are two segments in declaration order
GET /compare/1/2
>>> 200
~ compare 1 with 2

### a page with only optional parameters takes them all from the query
GET /search?query=lamps&page=3
>>> 200
~ search [lamps] page 3
~ no tag

### a page with only optional parameters renders its defaults without a query
GET /search
>>> 200
~ search [] page 1

### an optional Int that doesn't parse is a 404
GET /search?page=two
>>> 404

### an optional String? parameter is set from the query
GET /search?tag=red
>>> 200
~ tag [red]

### links omit optional parameters at their defaults and keep the others
GET /search?query=lamps
>>> 200
~ href="/search?query=lamps&amp;page=2"

### a Page parameter parses a path of this app
GET /proceed?returnTo=%2Fproduct%2F42%3Ftab%3Dreviews
>>> 200
~ continue to /product/42?tab=reviews

### a Page parameter at its default
GET /proceed
>>> 200
~ continue to /

### a Page parameter can't name another site
GET /proceed?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2F
>>> 404

### a protocol-relative Page parameter can't name another site
GET /proceed?returnTo=%2F%2Fevil.example%2F
>>> 404

### a Page parameter must name a page that exists
GET /proceed?returnTo=%2Fnowhere
>>> 404

### a renamed page's old URL redirects permanently
GET /plans
>>> 308
location: /pricing

### a redirect keeps the parameters of the renamed page
GET /product-page/42
>>> 308
location: /product/42

### a redirect keeps the query string
GET /product-page/42?tab=reviews
>>> 308
location: /product/42?tab=reviews

### a redirect from an old URL still parses its parameters
GET /product-page/abc
>>> 404

### HEAD of a redirect is a redirect
HEAD /plans
>>> 308
location: /pricing

### an unknown path is a 404
GET /nowhere/at/all
>>> 404
